318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Youth Convention is a gathering of student ministries within our Network for the purpose of drawing near to God in a high energy, Gospel centered, Spirit empowered environment. This event often ignites a passion for Christ that then is brought back to youth group. It is an opportunity for students to engage in corporate worship, a challenging biblical message and develop like-minded relationships with other students around them. Youth convention is a convention that happens annually for youth students only. Youth will be transported on a van to the location of youth convention and will stay overnight in a hotel with City Uth leadership team, including chaperones. There is a registration form, a photo/video release form, and a registration fee to complete before going on Youth Convention. City Uth leaders are required to attend Youth Convention and Fine Arts with students to help chaperone and support our students.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (SUMMER CAMP)
/E (SUMMER CAMP)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Summer Camp is a gathering of student ministries within our Network for the purpose of drawing near to God in a high energy, Gospel centered, Spirit empowered environment. Summer camp gives youth the opportunity to make new friends, have a camp counselor to mentor them, have fun through games, and to encounter the presence of God and experience breakthrough in a new way. Summer Camp is a Monday through Friday, overnight event. There is a registration form, a photo/video release form, and a medical release form to complete before attending camp. City Uth leaders have the opportunity to go as leaders to summer camp with students but are not required to. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
endobj
