>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Fine Arts is a discipleship tool of the Assemblies of God Youth Ministries designed to help students discover, develop, and deploy their ministry gifts. In a competitive venue, students throughout Southern New England are given the opportunity to have their skills evaluated by qualified ministers, industry professionals and educators who encourage excellence, offer ideas for improvement, and inspire students to use their gifts in the local church, community and around the world. By involving your students in Fine Arts, they will gain experience and develop skills that will last a lifetime. They are also able to obtain scholarships for faith-based colleges. Students can compete at the district-level competition, which happens at the same time as youth convention. If students pass the district level of competition, they advance to compete at the national level of the fine arts competition. City Uth leaders are required to attend Youth Convention and Fine Arts with students to help chaperone and support our students. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
